-- title:
--   Lifting ℓ-torsion homomorphisms to rational homomorphisms W→ X₀
-- statement:
--   Let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field with decidable equality, and let $X_0$ and $W$ be Weierstrass curves over $\kappa$ that are elliptic; base change of a curve over $\kappa$ along the identity of $\kappa$ is identified with the curve itself, so all point groups below are the affine point groups $X_0(\kappa)$ and $W(\kappa)$. Fix rationals $a,b$ and a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule $\Lambda$ of the quaternion algebra $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ which is an order in the sense of the project predicate [`QuaternionAlgebra.IsOrder`](def/QuaternionAlgebra_Order.html#L11), namely $1\in\Lambda$, $\Lambda$ is closed under multiplication, the $\mathbb{Q}$-span of $\Lambda$ is all of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$, and $\Lambda$ is finitely generated over $\mathbb{Z}$. Assume given a ring homomorphism $\theta$ from [`WeierstrassCurve.rationalEndSubring κ X₀`](def/WeierstrassCurve_RationalEnd.html#L32), the subring of $\operatorname{End}(X_0(\kappa))$ generated by the rational homomorphisms $X_0\to X_0$, into $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$, with $\theta$ injective and with range exactly $\Lambda$. Assume further an additive map $\chi\colon X_0(\kappa)\to W(\kappa)$ lying in [`WeierstrassCurve.rationalHomSet κ X₀ W`](def/WeierstrassCurve_RationalEnd.html#L28) (that is, $\chi=0$ or $\chi$ is given, off a finite set of $x$-coordinates, by ratios of bivariate polynomials in the coordinates), with $\chi\neq 0$, and a prime $\ell$ with $(\ell:\kappa)\neq 0$. Then for every additive map $f$ from the $\ell$-torsion submodule $\{P\in W(\kappa): \ell P=0\}$ to $X_0(\kappa)$ there exists $\rho$ in [`WeierstrassCurve.rationalHomSet κ W X₀`](def/WeierstrassCurve_RationalEnd.html#L28) with $\rho(P)=f(P)$ for all $\ell$-torsion points $P$ of $W(\kappa)$.
--
--   This is the surjectivity of reduction modulo $\ell$ of the group of rational homomorphisms $W\to X_0$ onto $\operatorname{Hom}(W[\ell],X_0(\kappa))$, available because the hypotheses force $\operatorname{Hom}(W,X_0)$ to have $\mathbb{Z}$-rank $4$ (through $\chi$ it becomes a left ideal of an order $\Lambda$ of rank $4$). It feeds the Čerednik–Drinfeld counting statement [`CerednikDrinfeld.natCard_subideal_primeHeckeSet_eq_natCard_subgroup_dualPair_of_kernelIdealSet`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.natCard_subideal_primeHeckeSet_eq_natCard_subgroup_dualPair_of_kernelIdealSet), where left ideals of the endomorphism order are matched with subgroups of the $\ell$-torsion.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_WeierstrassCurve_exists_mem_rationalHomSet_forall_torsionBy_apply_eq_of_rationalEndSubring_range_eq_quaternionOrder.lean

